# Task 3 Report — Optimizer Resource Ledger and Best-Effort Pricing

## Status

Completed and committed.

Commit: `09ed47675d211a4e20752a1f476c908ac8425ead` (`Use call-token ledger for PIT optimizer`)

No tests were added, modified, or run. No provider, Docker, hidden-data, network, push, upload, or subagent action was used.

## Behavior changed

- Added the dedicated `PitOptimizerResourceReservation`, `PitOptimizerResourceSnapshot`, and `PitOptimizerResourceLedger` runtime boundary.
- Optimizer reservations now enforce only API-call and conservative token capacity. `projected_cost_usd` is optional audit evidence, serialized as canonical decimal text or `null`, and is never compared to a ceiling.
- Before-send failures release the reserved call and tokens.
- Complete started calls require exact prompt/completion/total accounting and a finite non-negative actual cost. Actual tokens and authoritative USD are committed before a token-overage exception is reported.
- Incomplete started calls retain the full token reservation, increment incomplete accounting, record no invented cost, and make the resource ledger terminal to further reservations.
- Optimizer recovery state is schema v3 and contains calls/tokens, authoritative actual USD, optional projected cost evidence, active reservations, and reconciliations. It contains no optimizer `max_usd`, reserved USD, or retained-reservation USD shape.
- Generic `BudgetLedger`, `BudgetWindow`, diagnosis, proposal-batch, and legacy `pit_optimization` USD enforcement remain in place. Optimizer-only state and methods were removed from `BudgetLedger` after active optimizer callers were moved to the dedicated ledger.
- Pricing freeze now caches one run-bound `OptimizerPricingSnapshot`. Ordinary pricing-loader exceptions fall back to an authenticated unavailable snapshot while `BaseException` cancellation and expired deadlines retain precedence.
- Optimizer preflight validates role/model/lease identity plus byte/token bounds, returns `Decimal | None`, and does not gate on projected cost magnitude.
- The one-shot optimizer gateway forwards the same advisory projection to the resource and authorization reservations, preserves one provider attempt, strict model/schema/byte/accounting validation, and publishes schema-v3 provider/audit/recovery evidence without retained USD.
- Schema-v1/v2 provider serialization omits the newly added schema-v3 pricing field so legacy durable record shapes remain unchanged.

## Files changed

- `agent_loop.py`
  - Added the calls/tokens resource ledger and schema-v3 optimizer recovery/audit path.
  - Migrated optimizer pricing/preflight/gateway/live-composition call sites to `OptimizerPricingSnapshot` and advisory projections.
  - Preserved generic USD accounting and enforcement.
- `core/pit_optimizer_authorization.py`
  - Narrow authorized seam only: `_bind_gateway_lifecycle_commitment` now uses `PitOptimizerResourceLedger._pit_optimizer_reservation_primitive` instead of the hard-bound generic ledger serializer.

## Unavoidable Task-4-adjacent compatibility edit

`_build_pit_optimizer_v2_config` no longer passes `max_usd` into `PitOptimizerGateConfig`, because the dependency's schema-v3 constructor has already removed that field. Local live-run callback annotations and calls were minimally adapted to the new pricing/lease interfaces so `agent_loop.py` compiles. Broader controller/CLI naming and result-summary migration remains assigned to Task 4; existing `v2` function/parameter names were intentionally left in place.

